# .env.ci — F-193 Batch 2. Copied to `.env` by the CI `regression` job
# (.github/workflows/ci.yml) so the per-service `test:regression` scripts, which run
# `dotenv -e ../../.env -- node dist/regression/run.js`, find a DATABASE_URL.
#
# The database name ends in `_test`, which F-101's guard
# (packages/test-harness/src/database-guard.ts) accepts as disposable — the regression
# suites wipe the whole schema with unscoped deletes. The CI Postgres service container
# is ephemeral and created fresh per run; nothing here is a secret.
#
# JWT_SECRET is still deliberately omitted: the test harness and every service fall back to
# the same hardcoded value when it's unset, so leaving it out keeps both sides consistent.
#
# F-298: INTERNAL_SERVICE_KEY can no longer be omitted here. Every service now calls
# assertInternalServiceKeyConfigured() at startup (packages/shared-middleware) and refuses to
# boot with it unset -- the previous "fall back to a hardcoded value" behavior this comment
# used to describe was itself the fail-open gap F-298 closed. This value is CI-only, not a
# real secret, matching deploy/gcp-vm/.env.ci's own placeholder.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/badminton_db_test?schema=public
INTERNAL_SERVICE_KEY=ci-internal-service-key
